summary: Slow-operation log: what took seconds, and where the time went

!! Reference

```
Slow-operation log: what took seconds, and where the time went

Usage: mf slow [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list    List the slow operations, newest first — the default
  replay  Run a query again and show where its time goes, now: the newest logged query, the one logged at --at, or one typed with -q. Not itself logged
  clear   Empty the log (the clean slate a reproduction starts from)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
```
